1
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:13,940
I fear that the world will not accept
her, but she is a part of it all the same.

2
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,037
The true human, like anyone else.

3
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,517
It was a success.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,260
This is the first step.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,957
I'm confident that this will bring
peace to this planet someday.

6
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,880
Sign Dr.

7
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:29,217
Vegapunk, direct to Rodman's.

8
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,980
It's a laboratory for peace.

9
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:03,420
Thank you.

10
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,473
We're all set to take out the Vegapunks.

11
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,501
We've got them trapped like rats.

12
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:15,680
Now then, how do we drag
the rats from their nest?

13
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:18,520
That frontier dump
won't be easy to breach.

14
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,273
Yeah, tell me about it.

15
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:25,040
You know the Navy's rules about
attacking Emperors, don't you?

16
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:29,220
I don't acknowledge
Straw Hat as an Emperor.

17
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,500
Suit yourself, then.

18
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,720
They move quickly.

19
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,057
All of the sailing routes are blocked.

20
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:44,316
They've likely seized every
ship on the island by now.

21
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,802
We still have Vega Force One, but
it can't operate beyond Egghead.

22
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,054
They've turned our lab into a kill zone

23
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:56,180
Who will do the killing?

24
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:57,697
Time to avenge Atlas, gang?

25
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,897
Our objective right now is to escape!

26
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,297
Not to engage them!

27
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:04,897
But even so, a battle may be inevitable.

28
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:06,080
What's that?

29
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,717
I wasn't listening.

30
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,437
I gave myself chills.

31
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,177
Oh, hey, Lilith, buddy?

32
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,517
I don't think they can
even get up here right now.

33
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,117
So let's just put a pin
in the whole killing idea!

34
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,360
And cool our collective jets. Yeah?

35
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,980
Enough, Lilith.

36
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:23,284
Charging in blindly will
only make things worse.

37
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:26,157
Did you lose your spine or something?

38
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:29,437
These butt wipes are trying to take us
out and you don't even want to fight back?

39
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,520
What's your deal?

40
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,740
You are losing sight of our goal.

41
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,588
We need to get Stella
safely off the island.

42
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,557
We're not getting anywhere with
the whole armada in the way.

43
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,580
No, no.

44
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,697
Everyone just settle down, please.

45
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:44,297
We are Stella's satellites.

46
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:48,100
Our duty is to ensure his
safety even at our own peril.

47
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,073
We need to keep our priorities straight.

48
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,300
You running wild won't help anything.

49
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:00,661
This goody-two-shoes shit
is gonna get you killed.

50
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,720
And I won't miss ya. Just saying.

51
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,840
Yes. Noted.

52
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:09,750
Eureka!

53
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,817
I just thought of another invention!

54
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,940
But what can I -

55
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:17,997
I don't have enough time
or resources or manpower!

56
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,437
to conduct the research!

57
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,120
Where's my asses to be?

58
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,471
Oh, you were right there.

59
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,880
That's meowsic to my ears, Joshu!

60
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:31,820
Oh, poor Sentomaru, you took my side
and ended up like this. I'm sorry.

61
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,299
What should we do?

62
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:37,137
There is one other person on this
island who we could call for help.

63
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,257
We can't just expose our friend like that!

64
00:04:40,340 --> 00:04:41,797
The government would start a manhunt!

65
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,217
We need to punk up and
handle these ourselves.

66
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,820
I suppose you're right.

67
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,160
Anyway, that's the situation.

68
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:52,200
I can't leave because I'm
stuck in the lab. Stella, no!

69
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:54,916
Making that call is a death sentence!

70
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:55,910
Stop!

71
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:00,617
Now that you know the stakes, I
require your help out of this mess.

72
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,560
How could you?

73
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,819
Have you no shame?

74
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,179
Of course, Doctor.

75
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,757
I expected your call and I'm on the move.

76
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:07,670
Calick.

77
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,097
Did you hear that, everyone?

78
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,460
Help me, Zong's-a-vay!

79
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,869
Well, I guess we are
in a bit of a pickles.

80
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,897
Looks like we have no choice.

81
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:22,297
I don't feel great about this, but we need
someone to handle CP0 so we can escape!

82
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:26,020
Come on, guys, let's get Stella
on that ship! Works for me.

83
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:29,937
Then I'll take Vegaforce One and
carry the ship to one of the ports.

84
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:30,850
Good.

85
00:05:30,933 --> 00:05:31,837
Hurry and get it done.

86
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,777
What the hell is wrong with you?

87
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:36,537
You just can't resist
bossing everyone around, huh?

88
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:37,738
We're wasting time.

89
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,357
Let's begin the escape at once.

90
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,734
You're doing it again!

91
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,900
All right, seems we've got a plan.

92
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:48,257
I recrase our passage on your ship.

93
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:51,460
I assume there's enough
space. You know it. Let's go.

94
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:56,680
That is to say, I recrase our room
for seven. For seven? Ah, sweet!

95
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,717
The other Vegapunks are coming, too?

96
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:02,340
Seven of the world's best
scientists on my ship!

97
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:05,920
Are you kidding me?

98
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,337
This deal keeps getting worse and worse.

99
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,920
All of the Vegapunks are coming with us?

100
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:15,400
So then, that means we get
another lady on the ship?

101
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,280
Welcome to the team, Millet!

102
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:21,100
I'm so happy to have you with us!

103
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,110
Vegapunk!

104
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:32,020
I'm gonna squish you
like a bug! What a mess!

105
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,617
She forgot why she was mad!

106
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,497
All she can think about
now are those bugs!

107
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,410
Funny!

108
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,775
Please don't kick Mr.

109
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,750
Appelman's ass!

110
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,277
I said I'd help him escape!

111
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:42,157
Can you at least wait till later?

112
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,360
No, he's dead!

113
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,440
That sounds bad.

114
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:55,140
Labophase Defense System,
Frontier Dome now deactivated.

115
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:59,440
Labophase Defense System,
Frontier Dome now deactivated.

116
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:01,290
What?

117
00:07:01,373 --> 00:07:02,317
Who could have done this?

118
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,635
And for what purpose?

119
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:05,413
Talk to me, Pythagoras!

120
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,481
What's going on?

121
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:07,680
I don't know.

122
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,777
The interception protocol was
lifted without any warning.

123
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:11,940
We're wide open.

124
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:15,697
If the enemy heads for the
Labophase now, we can't stop them.

125
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:16,610
Damn it!

126
00:07:16,693 --> 00:07:17,523
Check the control room!

127
00:07:17,606 --> 00:07:18,436
Is anyone in there?

128
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:19,500
Control room?

129
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,620
Control room? It's empty!

130
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:25,980
I don't know how, but it seems the
barrier was deactivated remotely!

131
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,288
Who could have pulled
off a stunt like that?

132
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,860
Frontier Dome has been deactivated.

133
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:40,580
Did something happen
up there? Let's hurry.

134
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,429
This is our chance, right?

135
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,660
Who cares why? I do.

136
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,100
Could be a trap.

137
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,660
Or it could be our only opening.

138
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,194
We would be fools to let it pass us by.

139
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,797
This is entirely too convenient.

140
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,520
I know we want in there.

141
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,677
We can't complete our
mission if the barrier's up.

142
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:02,117
Trap or not, this is an
improvement in my book.

143
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:06,077
I'm going for it you snooze you lose

144
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,337
there

145
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:14,420
see

146
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:19,590
that lemon

147
00:08:19,673 --> 00:08:20,737
squeezy and nobody?

148
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:25,737
Exploded what do you know well it wasn't
a trap let's bust the door down and go!

149
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:30,077
Get them this is our golden opportunity
now wolves are at your door!

150
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:34,240
Poor Vegapunk, fortune has failed
you at the worst possible time.

151
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:40,278
Is that Straw Hat's ship over there?

152
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,857
I see now.

153
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:46,757
That's why it wasn't on
the coast when we arrived.

154
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,520
A giant robot too?

155
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,820
It's an eyesword. Destroy it.

156
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:53,180
I'll be done in a jiffy.

157
00:08:58,060 --> 00:08:59,797
And that takes care of the dishes.

158
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:03,577
Looks like I've still got plenty of
time, so I think I'll swab the deck next.

159
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:07,836
I should probably look into that
ominous alarm, but I'm sure it's fine.

160
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:26,540
Impicc-kick-gay-slicer!

161
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,240
What the hell?

162
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,853
Pearl, what's going on?

163
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:50,196
Are we under attack?

164
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,820
Who was that?

165
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,492
Can't you see I was trying to take a nap?

166
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,330
Roronoa!

167
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,560
Shaka! Code Red!

168
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:06,113
The Frontier Dome is up again,
but CP0 is already inside!

169
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,857
Damn it. We're too late.

170
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:12,587
They're trying to destroy
the Straw Hat ship.

171
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:17,320
Yes, but lucky for us, a few crew
members stayed behind to protect it.

172
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:20,697
We need to send backup.

173
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:23,420
If we don't, we'll lose our only escape!

174
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:32,077
Well, well, seems violence is the answer.

175
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,597
Now step back and leave
the feds to kill it.

176
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,577
And let you jeopardize everyone's safety?

177
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:37,820
Not a chance.

178
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,780
Bonnie, sure took off.

179
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:45,520
Where'd she go?

180
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,110
Hey!

181
00:10:49,193 --> 00:10:50,300
We're here, guys!

182
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:51,650
Huh?

183
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:54,420
Luffy! Chopper!

184
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:55,950
Geefey!

185
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:02,820
Oh, man!

186
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,117
You wouldn't believe all
the cool stuff we saw!

187
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,318
Even found a robot!

188
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,857
We agreed to take all
the Vegapunks with us.

189
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,680
We'd better hurry up! Aw!

190
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,440
But we just got here!

191
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,837
We haven't even seen the whole lab yet!

192
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,577
Can't we stay a little longer?

193
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,700
Maybe if you want to get murdered.

194
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:22,257
Look, we'd love to stay, but
this is a government island.

195
00:11:22,340 --> 00:11:23,780
Also, Lucci is here.

196
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:25,160
We hate that guy.

197
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,560
What was that?

198
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:30,995
He came from outside.

199
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,537
Cipherpole will show up any second now.

200
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:35,417
We'll get trapped in another fight.

201
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,880
Aw, come on.

202
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:40,220
Oh, have you guys seen Bonnie?

203
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,337
She's got long pink hair
and she's kind of mean.

204
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:44,420
Bonnie, huh? Huh?

205
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:47,337
Is that the girl you were
hanging with down in the city?

206
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,540
Yeah, that's her.

207
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:51,157
She's sort of trying to
kill Vegapunk right now.

208
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,070
What?

209
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:54,100
Why would she do that?

210
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,220
By the way, where is he?

211
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:58,120
He was here a second ago.

212
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,100
Die, Vegapunk!

213
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,250
Dammit!

214
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:12,440
Face me, you coward!

215
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,580
Get back here!

216
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,400
Stupid! Bonnie!

217
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,320
I don't have time for...

218
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,022
Please, please!

219
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,877
I do want to speak with
you, just without the...

220
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:30,420
Violence, if you don't mind, go to hell!

221
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,020
Bonnie! Woo!

222
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,080
I'm not letting you go!

223
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,917
You're going to look
me in the eye and tell

224
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,277
me if you can turn back my father or not!

225
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:46,500
Yes or no, live or die!

226
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:49,040
It's not that simple.

227
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:50,500
I'm sorry.

228
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:52,260
I can't.

229
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:54,166
Then you've made your choice!

230
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:06,580
This is for my father!

231
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,455
I have a good reason!

232
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,520
I promise you!

233
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,340
God damn it!

234
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:14,200
I don't know.

235
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,106
Something fell from the wall.

236
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,940
It's Bartholomew Kuma.

237
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,330
What?

238
00:14:27,413 --> 00:14:28,633
Where did he come from?

239
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:33,077
Actually, I think I heard in the
news that he escaped from Marie Joie.

240
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,680
But why is he here?

241
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:37,937
The Celestial Dragons called
him their invincible slave.

242
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:38,860
He's huge.

243
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:01,740
A former warlord of the sea,
Bartholomew Kuma, has appeared.

244
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:05,845
He's currently in the northeast,
near the entrance of Muldeross.

245
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:10,180
All Marines, dispatch immediately.

246
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,880
All citizens must evacuate the area.

247
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:24,757
Do not approach Cape
under any circumstance.

248
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,077
He's property of the Celestial Dragons.

249
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,560
He no longer has a human body.

250
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,937
His current programming is unknown.

251
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:36,320
Repeat, for your own safety, all
citizens must evacuate at once.

252
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,500
It hurts.

253
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:53,800
I must have broken my
leg when I fell down.

254
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,860
Oh, no.

255
00:15:59,020 --> 00:15:59,850
Zapoodle.

256
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,080
I'm going to get him.

257
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,713
They need the med team.

258
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:08,540
I'm sorry, Bonnie. Oh!

259
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,760
Distorted future!

260
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,440
Now you die!

261
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:28,840
I've been singled!

262
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:33,600
It's time to end it!

263
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,680
Please just listen, even if you can't be!

264
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,250
Change!

265
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:47,050
Now,

266
00:16:47,133 --> 00:16:53,780
sir,

267
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,217
why do I have to be a baby?

268
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,840
and bought us his gems.

269
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:09,020
Oh, my golden years.

270
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:10,450
Bonnie,

271
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:13,175
give back the shorty years of my life.

272
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,920
Stop your whining.

273
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:20,797
My powers don't work on
living things forever.

274
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,237
It'll wear off, but not
before we're done here.

275
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:24,600
Now out with it.

276
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,680
What was your good reason?

277
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,620
You said you had one.

278
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,500
So spit it out.

279
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:34,460
Why did you kill my father?

280
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:39,380
If I tell you, it will
only bring you more pain.

281
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:40,820
I'm sorry.

282
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,280
I want to help. I truly do.

283
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:45,520
But no! What?

284
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:51,680
I made a promise with
your father. You see?

285
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:57,560
Look, it's Kuma.

286
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:59,837
He's climbing straight up the red line.

287
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:03,391
Surely they're going to stop
him before he gets to the top.

288
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:16,440
Before he lost his humanity, I swore to him
that I'd never tell you why it happened.

289
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:27,660
You had a reason to kill my father,
but you can't say it? Screw you!

290
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:30,027
Who would believe that crap?

291
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,820
Do you think I'm stupid?

292
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:33,400
Of course I don't!

293
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:34,462
It's the truth!

294
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:37,180
So please let me go!

295
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:42,360
Kuma chose to give up
his humanity on his own!

296
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:43,760
It wasn't me!

297
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:47,740
It was his choice and no
one else's! You're lying!

298
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:50,440
You're saying he chose this hell?

299
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:52,380
That he chose to abandon me?

300
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:54,500
You killed him!

301
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,980
It was hell for me as well!

302
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,680
I can't even stand to remember it!

303
00:19:15,620 --> 00:19:18,497
Your father is an extraordinary man.

304
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:20,857
I'm proud to call him my friend.

305
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:23,077
I truly care for him.

306
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,097
I swear to you and that is exactly

307
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:30,280
why I won't please a word you bastard!

308
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:36,640
I'm sick of your self-serving lies.

309
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,724
I'm not gonna let you trick me.

310
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,560
This is abuse.

311
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:43,460
I can't take it.

312
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:53,660
It's just a broken contraption bunny.

313
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:56,660
It has nothing to do with Kuma, I promise.

314
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:58,760
Lying again.

315
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,920
OIL SHOCK, GO!

316
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:23,540
STUPID BODY!!!

317
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,640
You're wrong.

318
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:43,360
Please, no!

319
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:54,920
A person's thoughts? Indeed.

320
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:59,900
There was a scholar in the vest blue
who made a revolutionary discovery.

321
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:04,700
They said people lose 21 grams
of weight at the moment of death.

322
00:21:05,260 --> 00:21:09,080
So, you might say that's
the weight of a human soul.

323
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:13,420
Of course, there's much
more testing to do,

324
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:16,168
but I think it's proof
that the soul exists.

325
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:18,300
In fact, I'm certain of it.

326
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,654
I'm afraid this one might be beyond me.

327
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:27,960
On the contrary, you're an expert.

328
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,040
It is similar to your power.

329
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:38,320
A person's pain is illangible, yes?

330
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:43,260
But you can take it from their body
and transfer it to someone else.

331
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:51,351
Nerves create electrical signals, and
you can move them without using wires.

332
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,397
Let's compare it to mental images instead

333
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:03,817
mental images yes
memories and other images.

334
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:10,497
You see in your mind's eye are also
signals from nerve cells how much

335
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:15,857
do they weigh how Big are they that's
what i want to know fascinating

336
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:20,897
isn't it you want me to take out my
memories and Show them to you are

337
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:26,297
you trying to humiliate me i'm begging
you do it for the sake of science I

338
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:31,437
won't show them to anyone pretty
please forget it i could never trust

339
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,857
you with something as Sensitive as

340
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:39,397
that oh come now i must know stop it

341
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:45,037
you must not touch that pole it is
suffering In given form you could die

342
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:51,560
you know kuma's power the pain he
emerges is unbearable it will kill you

343
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:58,040
You're wrong it's not pain dad

344
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:10,160
Shoot Kuma down on sight!

345
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,106
He cannot reach Marie's wall!

346
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,140
Light him up!

347
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:29,420
All right, he's down!

348
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,230
Hurry!

349
00:23:36,313 --> 00:23:37,143
Surround him!

350
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:43,939
Evacuate the area!

351
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:44,962
It's dangerous!

352
00:23:56,300 --> 00:23:59,117
I know my father's power,

353
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:03,820
so I know what I'm seeing,

354
00:24:04,120 --> 00:24:05,420
and it isn't pain.

355
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,220
Finish him off!

356
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,460
Pull back!

357
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:21,240
The truth is, these are his memories.

358
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,470
What?

359
00:24:52,553 --> 00:24:54,540
How did Lucci get up here so fast?

360
00:24:54,900 --> 00:24:57,677
Unfortunately, it seems there
was a glitch in the system.

361
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,617
At least the Sunny will still be okay.

362
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:01,617
There's no way they'll
beat Zoro and Brook.

363
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:03,053
It's two against three.

364
00:25:03,260 --> 00:25:05,084
I wouldn't be so sure just yet.

365
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:08,097
No, look at the monitor.

366
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:10,945
I'm afraid their odds
are much worse than that.

367
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:16,137
No way the Seraphim are
here too it's two of

368
00:25:16,220 --> 00:25:18,777
your crew mates against
seven killing machines.

369
00:25:18,860 --> 00:25:24,020
We didn't order them to come up here
they're stuck with us either way.

370
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:27,797
The dome closed right after they came in.

371
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:33,517
Oh come on they snuck the Seraphim
in while the dome was down.

372
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:34,430
No fair.

373
00:25:34,513 --> 00:25:38,377
Actually I don't think CP0
intended to bring them here at all.

374
00:25:38,460 --> 00:25:39,340
Say what?

375
00:25:41,380 --> 00:25:42,917
It's a feature of the Seraphim.

376
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:46,882
In some circumstances, they can
make basic decisions on their own.

377
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:52,677
They must have figured out that the
Dome would be back soon and made a move.

378
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:55,337
Yes, but this could work in our favor.

379
00:25:55,420 --> 00:25:57,244
We can turn this battle around.

380
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:00,477
How would we do that?

381
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:03,384
They've got us backed
into a corner, don't they?

382
00:26:05,120 --> 00:26:09,260
Our orders outrank Gates on the
Seraphim scale of authority.

383
00:26:09,740 --> 00:26:12,940
Once we reach them, they'll answer to us.

384
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:34,897
Then we better get over there and give
them some orders before it's too late.

385
00:26:34,980 --> 00:26:37,200
Hang on, I'm coming, straw heads!

386
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:39,920
Hey, wait for me!

387
00:26:42,940 --> 00:26:44,705
Are you taking this seriously?

388
00:26:44,980 --> 00:26:46,620
Of course I am! Good!

389
00:26:46,900 --> 00:26:48,900
Let's hope those two can hold out.

390
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,110
Don't dawdle.

391
00:26:50,193 --> 00:26:51,417
We're counting on you two.

392
00:26:51,500 --> 00:26:52,330
Hey, no!

393
00:26:52,413 --> 00:26:53,379
You're not a boss!

394
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:55,250
Zoro!

395
00:26:55,333 --> 00:26:57,967
I've got to hit you with
everything I've got!

396
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:00,340
Oh, this is bad!

397
00:27:00,540 --> 00:27:03,457
Even Zoro and Brooke can't
take on all of them at once!

398
00:27:03,540 --> 00:27:05,497
In that case, I'll go back them up!

399
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:07,051
Good luck out there, pal!

400
00:27:07,180 --> 00:27:08,827
I'm just gonna hide in here!

401
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:10,537
I mean, guard the base!

402
00:27:10,620 --> 00:27:13,557
Guess Moss Head won't live
to see the One Piece, huh?

403
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,470
What a shame.

404
00:27:14,553 --> 00:27:16,117
Your crewmates need you, you idiot!

405
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,553
Get out there and help!

406
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:22,020
Did my darling Nami just
give me an order? I'm on it!

407
00:27:23,060 --> 00:27:25,460
Consider me your own personal seraphim!

408
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:28,704
Sanji Fem is here to do
anything you ask him to!

409
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,510
Wait!

410
00:27:30,593 --> 00:27:32,160
Why do I have to save Moss Head?

411
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,264
Because we need him, Curly Fem!

412
00:27:34,700 --> 00:27:36,288
Now come on, we gotta burn!

413
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:44,420
This is a lucky break.

414
00:27:44,900 --> 00:27:47,665
I've been waiting to
settle the score with you.

415
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:51,000
Time for round two.

416
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:53,830
Ready?

417
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:55,340
Let's go!

418
00:27:56,900 --> 00:27:57,820
Hold on.

419
00:27:57,980 --> 00:27:59,568
I thought he was a giraffe.

420
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:01,597
That's what he's supposed to be.

421
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,974
But I guess he does look kind of weird.

422
00:28:04,500 --> 00:28:05,400
Well, whatever.

423
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,840
He's getting cut down either way.

424
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:10,280
You think it'll be that easy, do you?

425
00:28:10,620 --> 00:28:11,660
Just try me!

426
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:14,500
Look after the ship, okay?

427
00:28:14,780 --> 00:28:15,640
Roger that.

428
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:17,134
You better not flinch!

429
00:28:17,580 --> 00:28:18,680
Nose pistol!

430
00:28:23,700 --> 00:28:25,180
That's just a sample.

431
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:26,948
Here comes the main course.

432
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,160
Tarrasque blast!

433
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:32,421
Plenty more where that came from!

434
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:47,660
This isn't anything new to me.

435
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:51,380
I fought a guy with a
long neck in Wano, too.

436
00:28:52,860 --> 00:28:55,640
Now get the hell away from our ship!

437
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:15,537
We'll take out the lab
and Vegapunk with it!

438
00:29:15,620 --> 00:29:17,320
Destroy everything in sight!

439
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:36,150
No!

440
00:29:36,233 --> 00:29:38,198
The Seraphim are aiming for the lab!

441
00:29:57,720 --> 00:29:58,680
We're trapped!

442
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:02,360
If our allies fail, we'll all
be crushed! What? Crushed?

443
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:25,520
Oh, no.

444
00:30:26,660 --> 00:30:30,601
Whether you defeat me or not,
there's no getting out of this alive.

445
00:30:30,940 --> 00:30:33,780
Really showboating
today, aren't you, kids?

446
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:35,280
Those bastards.

447
00:30:44,340 --> 00:30:47,811
Keep this up, and we'll have
the mission done before lunch!

448
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:04,400
Stussy, you...

449
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:19,430
Kaku!

450
00:31:23,060 --> 00:31:25,200
Stussy, what are you doing?

451
00:31:26,320 --> 00:31:27,380
Answer me!

452
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:31,020
Oh, nothing.

453
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:34,280
Just putting a bad boy to sleep.

454
00:31:38,580 --> 00:31:40,480
Do me a favor, Lucci.

455
00:31:41,540 --> 00:31:43,920
Why don't you join him?

456
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:11,117
That's gotta be the biggest
fish I've ever seen!

457
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:14,376
They say there's something
unusual about these waters.

458
00:32:14,620 --> 00:32:16,120
This should be fun.

459
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,180
Is that an island?

460
00:32:19,760 --> 00:32:21,020
Kid, wake up.

461
00:32:22,300 --> 00:32:23,840
We've got land up ahead.

462
00:32:24,420 --> 00:32:25,714
Should we drop anchor?

463
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:27,460
That's a dumb question.

464
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:30,077
We've made it this far, haven't we?

465
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:32,572
So there's no island left for us to fear.

466
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:34,580
Hold up. Wait.

467
00:32:34,900 --> 00:32:36,220
The hell is that?

468
00:32:40,060 --> 00:32:42,060
I think I might know where we are.

469
00:32:43,660 --> 00:32:46,360
It's the island of the giants, Elbath.

470
00:32:49,320 --> 00:32:50,150
Interesting.

471
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:54,760
Absolutely not.

472
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,118
Are you kidding me?

473
00:32:56,300 --> 00:32:59,057
We're headed out for the
Egghead mission any minute now.

474
00:32:59,140 --> 00:33:02,137
I'm not going to lend you my
troops at a time like this.

475
00:33:02,220 --> 00:33:05,514
Are they too busy removing
that stick from your caboose?

476
00:33:07,740 --> 00:33:09,320
Laugh it up all you want.

477
00:33:09,540 --> 00:33:10,820
My answer's still no.

478
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,597
Besides, that island's an emperor's turf.

479
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,562
Did you get clearance to invade?

480
00:33:15,680 --> 00:33:17,657
I bet the brass popped
a vein when you asked.

481
00:33:17,740 --> 00:33:19,540
I have to ask.

482
00:33:20,460 --> 00:33:21,290
Huh?

483
00:33:21,373 --> 00:33:23,662
Come on, how many decades
have you been a marine?

484
00:33:25,700 --> 00:33:26,920
It'll all work out.

485
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:28,720
I'm here, by the way.

486
00:33:29,020 --> 00:33:29,880
Wait, what?

487
00:33:32,220 --> 00:33:33,260
El Mabo!

488
00:33:34,820 --> 00:33:36,620
Get your butt out here!

489
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:38,070
What?

490
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,880
Is it a pirate?

491
00:33:40,100 --> 00:33:42,717
It sounds like they've come
here to take revenge on Helmepo.

492
00:33:42,800 --> 00:33:44,240
No. Wait!

493
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:51,980
Oh, good!

494
00:33:52,400 --> 00:33:53,518
There you are, boy!

495
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:55,193
Didn't keep me waiting.

496
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:57,220
My central guard!

497
00:33:59,100 --> 00:34:00,877
I'm so glad you're here!

498
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:04,480
Gobi got caught by Blackbeard.

499
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,297
It wasn't his fault.

500
00:34:06,380 --> 00:34:09,260
He was so brave, but I was helpless.

501
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:11,020
I couldn't do anything.

502
00:34:11,620 --> 00:34:13,914
Would you stop your blubbering already?

503
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,460
You look like a fool.

504
00:34:17,160 --> 00:34:19,300
I just want to help them.

505
00:34:20,740 --> 00:34:22,000
Glad to hear it.

506
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:23,420
Hop aboard.

507
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:25,020
Pirate Island?

508
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:28,017
You think that'll scare
off an old marine like me?

509
00:34:28,100 --> 00:34:30,877
We'll give those bastards a
beating on their own turf.

510
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:34,640
We're going to kick down their
front door and rescue Kali!

511
00:34:35,420 --> 00:34:36,900
I said broken!

512
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:07,360
I'm always looking at my head in my head.

513
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:08,790
I'm still looking for the future!

514
00:35:08,873 --> 00:35:13,597
I'm looking for

515
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:18,740
a real promise.

516
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:23,217
I'm in my heart.

517
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:25,760
I'm in my heart.
